---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Comments from '../../components/Comments.astro';
const P = 'https://media.huanyuchen.com/misc/wangcai/';
---
<BaseLayout title="Wangcai — Huanyu Chen"
  description="Our dog Wangcai, month by month from her foster week in December 2024 to November 2026: where she sleeps, what she plays with, the whipped cream, the beaches and trails of Orange County, the back seat, and the costumes.">
  <p class="muted"><a href="/misc">← Misc</a> · December 2024 – November 2026</p>
  <h1>Wangcai</h1>
  <p class="muted trip-sub">Twenty-four months of our dog, mostly through my wife's camera.</p>

  <div class="callout trip-stats">
    <strong>24 months · December 2024 – November 2026</strong><br />
    one foster week · one adoption in Boston · a donut bed, a sofa and a teepee · a yellow duck and a yellow octopus ·
    whipped cream, an empty yogurt tub and one cake · Huntington Dog Beach, Crystal Cove and the hills of Irvine · a lot of
    back seat · a bee, a hot dog, Sherlock Holmes and a blonde wig
  </div>

  <p>
    This post is about our dog, Wangcai. How she came to us is its own story: a foster week in Los Angeles in December
    2024, a month in which she was supposed to be someone else's dog, and then a shelter listing in Boston that sent
    my wife, and a week later me, across the country to bring her home. That story, and where her name comes from, is in
    <a href="/misc/wangcai-2025">Bringing Wangcai Home</a>. This post is everything since.
  </p>
  <p>
    Most of the photos here are my wife's. She takes far more pictures of Wangcai than I do, and a large share of
    her camera roll from these two years is the dog: asleep, on a walk, in a hat. I went through it month by month
    and kept what the photos show. Where I was there too, I say "we"; some of these walks were just the two of them.
  </p>

  <h2 id="months">Twenty-four months</h2>
  <p>
    One photo for every month, from the foster week to this one. The first is from December 2024, when she was still
    Muffin and only staying with us for a week; the second is from her first evening back in Los Angeles in January,
    asleep in her yellow pajamas.
  </p>
  <figure class="trip-fig">
    <div class="month-grid">
      <div class="mcell"><img src={P + 'm-2024-12.webp'} alt="Wangcai on a leash under a tree wrapped in white lights at night." loading="lazy" /><span>Dec 2024</span></div>
      <div class="mcell"><img src={P + 'm-2025-01.webp'} alt="Wangcai asleep in yellow pajamas on a fluffy grey blanket." loading="lazy" /><span>Jan 2025</span></div>
      <div class="mcell"><img src={P + 'm-2025-02.webp'} alt="A close portrait of Wangcai smiling, ears up." loading="lazy" /><span>Feb 2025</span></div>
      <div class="mcell"><img src={P + 'm-2025-03.webp'} alt="Wangcai sitting on a rainbow-striped rug in a yellow bib." loading="lazy" /><span>Mar 2025</span></div>
      <div class="mcell"><img src={P + 'm-2025-04.webp'} alt="Wangcai lying on the carpet, chewing, with a bone toy beside her." loading="lazy" /><span>Apr 2025</span></div>
      <div class="mcell"><img src={P + 'm-2025-05.webp'} alt="Wangcai on a pink leash on a sandy beach at sunset." loading="lazy" /><span>May 2025</span></div>
      <div class="mcell"><img src={P + 'm-2025-06.webp'} alt="Wangcai lying on a striped rug in a plaid deerstalker hat and cape." loading="lazy" /><span>Jun 2025</span></div>
      <div class="mcell"><img src={P + 'm-2025-07.webp'} alt="Wangcai sitting on the carpet, tongue out, looking up." loading="lazy" /><span>Jul 2025</span></div>
      <div class="mcell"><img src={P + 'm-2025-08.webp'} alt="Wangcai lying on a red sofa, looking at the camera." loading="lazy" /><span>Aug 2025</span></div>
      <div class="mcell"><img src={P + 'm-2025-09.webp'} alt="Wangcai sitting on a wooden deck at sunset." loading="lazy" /><span>Sep 2025</span></div>
      <div class="mcell"><img src={P + 'm-2025-10.webp'} alt="Wangcai in a plaid cap and dark coat on a beach path, looking back." loading="lazy" /><span>Oct 2025</span></div>
      <div class="mcell"><img src={P + 'm-2025-11.webp'} alt="Wangcai on a pink leash at the edge of the water on a beach." loading="lazy" /><span>Nov 2025</span></div>
      <div class="mcell"><img src={P + 'm-2025-12.webp'} alt="Wangcai lying on a striped blanket next to a green plush toy, tongue out." loading="lazy" /><span>Dec 2025</span></div>
      <div class="mcell"><img src={P + 'm-2026-01.webp'} alt="Wangcai with her nose in a small decorated cake." loading="lazy" /><span>Jan 2026</span></div>
      <div class="mcell"><img src={P + 'm-2026-02.webp'} alt="Wangcai in bed with a yellow plush octopus draped over her head." loading="lazy" /><span>Feb 2026</span></div>
      <div class="mcell"><img src={P + 'm-2026-03.webp'} alt="Wangcai in a yellow bandana printed with the word PUP." loading="lazy" /><span>Mar 2026</span></div>
      <div class="mcell"><img src={P + 'm-2026-04.webp'} alt="Wangcai sitting in the back seat of a car, tongue out." loading="lazy" /><span>Apr 2026</span></div>
      <div class="mcell"><img src={P + 'm-2026-05.webp'} alt="Wangcai in a pink gingham bucket hat and matching bandana." loading="lazy" /><span>May 2026</span></div>
      <div class="mcell"><img src={P + 'm-2026-06.webp'} alt="Wangcai on a dirt trail between dry grass and a wooden fence." loading="lazy" /><span>Jun 2026</span></div>
      <div class="mcell"><img src={P + 'm-2026-07.webp'} alt="Wangcai sniffing the grass above a bay at sunset." loading="lazy" /><span>Jul 2026</span></div>
      <div class="mcell"><img src={P + 'm-2026-08.webp'} alt="Wangcai curled up in a white duvet on a hotel bed." loading="lazy" /><span>Aug 2026</span></div>
      <div class="mcell"><img src={P + 'm-2026-09.webp'} alt="Wangcai in a hot-dog costume, tongue out." loading="lazy" /><span>Sep 2026</span></div>
      <div class="mcell"><img src={P + 'm-2026-10.webp'} alt="Wangcai in a pink cowboy hat and pink bandana, sitting on a rug." loading="lazy" /><span>Oct 2026</span></div>
      <div class="mcell"><img src={P + 'm-2026-11.webp'} alt="Wangcai buried in sand up to her neck, only her head showing." loading="lazy" /><span>Nov 2026</span></div>
    </div>
    <figcaption>One photo a month. Places, left to right: downtown Los Angeles; the Wedge in Newport Beach (May 2025);
      Crystal Cove (Sep 2025); Long Beach (Oct 2025); Huntington Dog Beach (Nov 2025 and Nov 2026); Newport Beach
      (Mar 2026); the hills of Irvine (Jun 2026); Upper Newport Bay (Jul 2026); Santa Cruz (Aug 2026). April 2026 is in
      the car and September 2026 on an outing; the rest are at home.</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <p>
    Looking at them in a row, a few things repeat. She is almost always looking straight at the camera. She has a lot
    of hats. And many of them are outdoors, on the beaches and hills of Orange County. The sections below follow
    those threads.
  </p>
  <p>
    The hats and bandanas deserve a note of their own, since they are in five of the twenty-four. In June 2025 it was a brown
    plaid deerstalker with a cape, which made her Sherlock Holmes for the evening. On March 18, 2026, at a sidewalk
    table in Newport Beach, she wore a yellow bandana printed with the word PUP. On May 11, 2026, a little after
    midnight, it was a pink gingham bucket hat with a bandana to match, and in October 2026 a pink cowboy hat.
  </p>
  <p>
    A few of the months are trips. The August 2026 photo is from the <a href="/misc/tahoe-2026">Tahoe loop</a>: at four
    minutes to midnight on August 25, in our room in Santa Cruz, she was curled up in the middle of the white duvet. The
    December 2024 photo is from the foster week, on an evening walk in downtown Los Angeles under a tree wrapped in
    white lights, near the end of that week.
  </p>

  <h2 id="asleep">Asleep</h2>
  <p>
    A large share of the photos are of Wangcai asleep. She has a grey donut bed, and one way she uses it is
    upside down, with all four legs in the air and her head tipped back over the rim. This one is from 8:43 one
    morning in July 2025.
  </p>
  <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'sleep-upside-down.webp'} alt="Wangcai asleep upside down in a round grey dog bed, legs in the air." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The donut bed, July 15, 2025, 8:43 am.</figcaption></figure>
  <p>
    Another is under the covers. In January 2026 she was photographed at 1:25 in the morning wrapped in a
    beige blanket so that only her face showed, and in March 2025 my wife photographed her from very close, head on
    the pillow, nose first.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'sleep-blanket.webp'} alt="Wangcai's face peeking out of a beige blanket." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>January 28, 2026, 1:25 am.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'sleep-nose.webp'} alt="A close-up of Wangcai's nose and eyes, her head resting on a pillow." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Nose first, March 28, 2025.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>

  <h2 id="toys">Toys</h2>
  <p>
    Her toys in these photos are plush and mostly yellow or green. She also has a white teepee, and on the evening of
    October 21, 2026 she was lying inside it with her head on a big yellow plush duck. In April 2026 she was shaking a
    green one hard enough that the photo came out as a blur of fur and felt.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'teepee-duck.webp'} alt="Wangcai lying in a white teepee with her head on a large yellow plush duck." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The teepee and the duck, October 21, 2026.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'green-plush.webp'} alt="A motion-blurred Wangcai with a green plush toy in her mouth." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>April 12, 2026.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>

  <h2 id="treats">Whipped cream, yogurt and a cake</h2>
  <p>
    During her foster week she discovered the little cups of whipped cream that coffee shops give to dogs, and that has
    not changed. On November 2, 2026, at an outdoor table at a Starbucks, she sat next to her cup.
  </p>
  <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'pup-cup.webp'} alt="Wangcai sitting at an outdoor table next to a Starbucks drink and a small cup of whipped cream." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>A pup cup, November 2, 2026, 1:59 pm.</figcaption></figure>
  <p>
    At home, the equivalent is an empty yogurt tub. In May 2026, just before one in the morning, she had one between her
    paws and was licking it clean. I took a photo of the same moment.
  </p>
  <figure class="trip-fig narrow-fig"><img src={P + 'yogurt-tub.webp'} alt="Wangcai lying on the carpet licking the inside of a yogurt tub held between her paws." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>May 8, 2026.</figcaption></figure>
  <p>
    Nobody knows her real birthday, so we count the day she was adopted as her birthday. On January 17, 2026, a year
    to the day after my wife picked her up from the MSPCA in Boston, she had her first birthday cake: a dog cake
    covered in sugar flowers, with a paw print and the letters MUFFIN, her name from the foster week, on top. A few
    minutes later her face was in it.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'cake.webp'} alt="A small round dog cake with sugar flowers, a paw print and the word MUFFIN." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Her first birthday, January 17, 2026, 5:37 pm.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'm-2026-01.webp'} alt="Wangcai with her nose in the cake." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>5:41 pm.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>

  <h2 id="outside">Sand, grass and one patch of snow</h2>
  <p>
    The walks in these photos are mostly along the Orange County coast: the bluffs at Crystal Cove, Upper Newport
    Bay, and <strong>Huntington Dog Beach</strong>, the dog beach in Huntington Beach. On November 1, 2025 she stood at the
    waterline and watched the waves; on a July morning in 2026 she lay in the grass above the beach; and on November 7,
    2026 she let herself be buried in the sand up to the neck, which is the last photo in the grid.
  </p>
  <p>
    Many of these walks are around sunset. On May 9, 2025 she was on the sand at the Wedge, at the tip of the Balboa Peninsula in
    Newport Beach, at 7:44 pm, with the sky going orange behind her. On September 19, 2025 she sat on a wooden deck
    above Crystal Cove at 6:50 pm. On July 6, 2026 she was nose-down in the grass on the bluffs over Upper Newport Bay,
    with the marsh and the water behind her, at 7:40 pm. All three are in the grid.
  </p>
  <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'huntington-grass.webp'} alt="Wangcai lying on green grass on a bluff, with a wooden fence and the ocean behind." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Above the beach in Huntington Beach, July 20, 2026, 9:49 am.</figcaption></figure>
  <p>
    Inland, the trails are the dry hills of Irvine. On September 6, 2025, a little before sunset, she was out on a
    dirt trail near Quail Hill, small in the middle of the path with the hills going gold around her. The June 2026
    photo in the grid is from the same hills.
  </p>
  <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'quail-hill-trail.webp'} alt="Wangcai standing on a wide dirt trail between dry brush, with hills in low evening light." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Near Quail Hill, Irvine, September 6, 2025, 6:29 pm.</figcaption></figure>
  <p>
    Snow is rare in these photos. One is from her first week with us, in Boston in January 2025, when my wife was
    there with her on her own, before I flew in: on the afternoon of January 23 she was standing in snow beside a
    tree, on a pink leash, with paw prints around her. Another is on the road, at Crater Lake.
  </p>
  <figure class="trip-fig narrow-fig"><img src={P + 'boston-snow.webp'} alt="Wangcai on a pink leash standing in fresh snow beside a tree trunk, paw prints around her." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Boston, January 23, 2025, 4:29 pm. My wife's photo, from their week there without me.</figcaption></figure>

  <h2 id="car">The back seat</h2>
  <p>
    Wangcai spends a lot of time in the back seat. In May 2025, on the evening of the first
    drive in our new car, we took her to the Wedge in Newport Beach for the sunset (May in the grid), and in the car
    she looked over the back seat at the camera, tongue out. In July she rode with her head by the window, watching the road
    go by.
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'car-cargo.webp'} alt="Wangcai looking over the back of a car seat, tongue out." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>May 9, 2025, 7:31 pm.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'car-window.webp'} alt="A close profile of Wangcai looking out of a car window." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>July 25, 2025.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>

  <h2 id="costumes">Dressing up</h2>
  <p>
    The hats in the grid are only part of the wardrobe. For Halloween 2025 she was a bee, in a striped body and a
    yellow hood with little wings.
    In October 2025 we also took her to Long Beach in a plaid cap and coat (October in the grid).
  </p>
  <div class="trip-pair">
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'bee-costume.webp'} alt="Wangcai lying on a wooden floor in a black-and-yellow bee costume with wings." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>A bee, October 31, 2025.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="trip-fig"><img src={P + 'blonde-wig.webp'} alt="Wangcai lying on a striped rug in an orange costume and a blonde wig." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>A blonde wig, October 12, 2026, 9:43 pm.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
  <p>
    In 2026 Halloween started early. On October 12 she tried on a blonde wig at home, on the 26th a pink cowboy hat
    and bandana, and on October 31 we took her to a Halloween dog-costume parade in Long Beach, in a diner uniform. By then Christmas had started too: on October 23 the giant tree at the
    Irvine Spectrum was already up and lit, and she stood under it.
  </p>
  <figure class="trip-fig narrow-fig"><img src={P + 'spectrum-tree.webp'} alt="Wangcai standing at night under a giant lit Christmas tree in an outdoor plaza." loading="lazy" /><figcaption>Irvine Spectrum, October 23, 2026, 7:59 pm.</figcaption></figure>

  <h2 id="road">On the road</h2>
  <p>
    Wangcai has come on many of our road trips since she came home, and those posts have more of her:
    the drive to <a href="/misc/phoenix-2025">Phoenix and Arcosanti</a> in March 2025, two months in;
    <a href="/misc/coast-weekends">Santa Barbara and the dunes</a> and the giant hands at
    <a href="/misc/joshua-tree">Joshua Tree</a> in the summer of 2025; a cabin weekend at
    <a href="/misc/big-bear-2025">Big Bear</a>; Labor Day in <a href="/misc/las-vegas">Las Vegas</a>; Thanksgiving
    in <a href="/misc/oregon-2025">Oregon</a>, with Crater Lake in snow; <a href="/misc/sedona-2026">Sedona</a> in
    January 2026; the <a href="/misc/spring-break-2026">spring-break loop</a> to the Bisti badlands and Red Rocks;
    my wife's drive up to the <a href="/misc/bay-area">Bay Area</a> with her in the summer of 2026; the
    <a href="/misc/tahoe-2026">Tahoe loop</a> in August 2026; and two visits to <a href="/misc/san-diego">San Diego</a>
    in October 2026. Closer to home, she is in <a href="/misc/irvine-oc">Irvine and Around</a>,
    <a href="/misc/la-outdoors">the LA hills</a>, on the pier beside the <a href="/misc/la-gardens">USS Iowa</a> and at
    the <a href="/misc/la-coast">Manhattan Beach pier</a>.
  </p>

  <p class="muted"><small>Photo locations have been removed from the published images, and where we live is never
    shown or named.</small></p>
  <p class="muted"><small>Some photos in this post are my wife's.</small></p>
  <Comments />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .trip-sub { margin-top: -.4em; font-size: 1.1rem; }
  .trip-stats { margin: 1.2em 0; line-height: 1.6; }
  .trip-fig { margin: 1.2em 0; }
  .trip-fig img { width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: 8px; display: block; }
  .trip-fig figcaption { color: var(--muted); font-size: .9rem; margin-top: .35em; text-align: center; }
  .narrow-fig { max-width: 420px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; }
  .trip-pair { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 12px; align-items: start; }
  .trip-pair .trip-fig { margin: .6em 0; }
  .month-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(6, 1fr); gap: 8px; }
  .month-grid .mcell { margin: 0; }
  .month-grid img { aspect-ratio: 1 / 1; object-fit: cover; border-radius: 6px; }
  .month-grid span { display: block; text-align: center; font-size: .78rem; color: var(--muted); margin-top: .2em; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .trip-pair { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .month-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
  }
</style>
